Vendored MaterialX standard libraries
=====================================

This directory contains a subset of the MaterialX standard libraries vendored
from the upstream MaterialX project.

Upstream:    https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/MaterialX
Tag:         v1.39.5
Source path: libraries/{stdlib,pbrlib,bxdf,nprlib}/*.mtlx

License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory).

Files included
--------------
- libraries/stdlib/stdlib_defs.mtlx
- libraries/stdlib/stdlib_ng.mtlx
- libraries/pbrlib/pbrlib_defs.mtlx
- libraries/pbrlib/pbrlib_ng.mtlx
- libraries/bxdf/standard_surface.mtlx
- libraries/bxdf/disney_principled.mtlx
- libraries/bxdf/open_pbr_surface.mtlx
- libraries/bxdf/usd_preview_surface.mtlx
- libraries/bxdf/gltf_pbr.mtlx
- libraries/nprlib/nprlib_defs.mtlx
- libraries/nprlib/nprlib_ng.mtlx

Files intentionally NOT included
--------------------------------
- libraries/targets/  (target-specific shader generation)
- libraries/cmlib/    (color management, handled in Rust directly)
- libraries/lights/   (lightshader-typed materials, this project uses its own
                       light system)
- libraries/bxdf/lama/ and libraries/bxdf/translation/
- per-target source directories under each library
  (genglsl/genosl/genmdl/genmsl/), since this project provides its own
  evaluator instead of using MaterialX shader generation.

The mtlx files are copied from the tag above, then a small set of local
compatibility patches is applied by `tools/update_materialx_libs`. To update,
check out the tag above in `third_party/MaterialX` and run
`cargo run --manifest-path tools/update_materialx_libs/Cargo.toml`.
